title: November 2024

@independence_2024
# prose-audit: Grade A — Malewski's march returns as a conflict among party organisers, public authority and exposed residents; a binding police standard now requires Lewica's Interior Ministry, while other government and opposition routes remain proposals backed by monitoring.
title: The 2024 Independence Day March
subtitle: Governing responsibility changes the street calculation
face-image: img/poland/events/independence-march-2021.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 20
order: 20
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2024 and month = 11
on-arrival: last_independence_march_year = 2024; far_right_street_capacity += 3; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += -5; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_backlash += 6

= November 2024 — Police, ministers and the counter-march

**Bartosz Malewski**, president of the Independence March Association, again
claims Warsaw's largest Independence Day procession for the nationalist
right. Police commanders prepare for the route; minority residents and legal
observers prepare for what may happen along it. The question for Lewica is no
longer whether the march exists, but which institution we are willing to put
beside it.

[? if civic_independence_years > 0: Our civic-independence organisers already
have mayors, unionists and democratic veterans capable of filling a square
without borrowing Malewski's stage.?] [? if independence_monitor_years > 0:
Our monitors have also accumulated evidence, lawyers and trust among people
who live along the route.?] [? if independence_join_years > 0: A
social-patriotic current has marched inside the main procession before and now
wants that foothold recognised as legitimate Lewica work.?]

[? if left_in_government = 1 and interior_minister_party = "Lewica": Lewica now
holds the Interior Ministry as well as a party banner. Interior Minister **[+
interior_minister +]** may issue a lawful operational standard for the police,
but cannot turn a partisan tactic into a command.?] [? if left_in_government =
1 and interior_minister_party != "Lewica": Lewica sits in cabinet without the
Interior Ministry. Our ministers may argue for a common standard in coalition
council; Interior Minister **[+ interior_minister +]**, serving for **[+
interior_minister_party +]**, still owns police instructions.?] [? if
left_in_government = 0: We remain in opposition. We can organise, monitor and
challenge Warsaw's decision, but the police will not take orders from our
party office.?]
[? if left_in_government = 1 and government_party = "pis": Service in a
PiS-led cabinet makes the boundary harsher: many coalition supporters call
Malewski's procession their own, while our voters expect Lewica ministers to
protect those in its path.?]

- @ind24_civic
- @ind24_join
- @ind24_rules
- @ind24_ban

@ind24_civic
title: Lead a civic-independence commemoration outside government protocol
subtitle: [? if civic_independence_investment >= 3: The institution now pays its own annual costs. No resource cost.?][? if civic_independence_investment < 3: Spend 1 resource.?] Give unions, veterans and mayors a patriotic institution of their own.
choose-if: civic_independence_investment >= 3 or resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The party organisation cannot stage a separate event.
on-arrival: resources -= 1 if civic_independence_investment < 3; civic_independence_investment += 1 if civic_independence_investment < 3; independence_march_strategy = "Civic tradition"; civic_independence_years += 1; civic_patriotism += 6; local_network += 2; public_trust += 2; far_right_street_capacity -= 1; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += 10; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_backlash += 4; news_headline = "The Left contests patriotism without commanding the police response"

Union banners, veterans of the democratic opposition and local choirs gather
under a committee independent of the day's police operation. [? if
left_in_government = 1: Our ministers attend only as party figures; the order
to protect both assemblies remains with public authorities.?] [? if
left_in_government = 0: Our opposition status is plain, but so is the capacity
to build something rather than merely petition the state.?]

Malewski keeps the larger procession. He no longer keeps the holiday's only
organised language of belonging, and local Lewica branches leave with an event
they can repeat next year.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the civic commemoration on the events desk

@ind24_join
title: Authorise a social-patriotic party column inside the main march
subtitle: Keep public office-holders away; gain the stage and own every incident around the column.
on-arrival: independence_march_strategy = "Join the Independence March"; independence_join_years += 1; civic_patriotism += 4; social_patriot_support += 9; left_cultural_position += 4; left_right_score += 4; rural_support += 2; progressives_dissent += 9; spring_dissent += 7; razem_dissent += 6; progressive_credibility -= 5; public_trust -= 2; government_coalition_dissent += 4 if left_in_government = 1; ko_relation -= 3 if left_in_government = 1; minority_safety -= 2; far_right_street_capacity += 2; far_right_fragmentation += 3; public_mood_pending_national_security_support += 5; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support -= 4; news_headline = "A social-patriotic Left column joins the march without government patronage"

The social-patriotic current enters beneath its own banner and finds an
audience for wages, public ownership and national dignity. Malewski can no
longer pretend that every marcher accepts his programme; he can still present
Lewica's presence as recognition of his event.

Progressive members and minority organisations judge us by the chants and
symbols surrounding the column, not only by the speech made inside it. [? if
left_in_government = 1: Keeping ministers away preserves the formal line
between party and state, but our coalition partners still inherit the
photographs.?] [? if left_in_government = 0: No ministry is implicated; the
party alone owns both the access and the damage.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Return the party column to the events desk

@ind24_rules
title: [? if left_in_government = 1 and interior_minister_party = "Lewica": Issue one policing and assembly standard for every march?][? if left_in_government = 0 or interior_minister_party != "Lewica": Publish one standard and force the Interior Ministry to answer it?]
subtitle: Apply the same lawful test to nationalists, counter-demonstrators and police—without inventing authority over the service.
on-arrival: {!
Q.independence_march_strategy = "Legal monitoring";
Q.independence_monitor_years += 1;
Q.constitutional_restraint += 4;
Q.minority_safety += 2;
if (Q.left_in_government && Q.interior_minister_party == "Lewica") {
    Q.police_trust += 4;
    Q.government_procedural_restraint += 3;
Q.public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += 5;
Q.public_mood_pending_national_security_salience += 4;
Q.public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += 8;
    Q.news_headline =
        "The Interior Ministry issues one neutral assembly standard";
} else {
    Q.media_capacity += 2;
    if (Q.left_in_government) {
        Q.government_procedural_restraint += 1;
    }
    Q.news_headline =
        "Lewica publishes an assembly standard the Interior Ministry must answer";
}
!}

[? if left_in_government = 1 and interior_minister_party = "Lewica": Interior
Minister **[+ interior_minister +]** issues written rules for route changes,
police intervention, evidence retention and the protection of
counter-demonstrators. Commanders receive a standard they can defend after the
crowd leaves, and Malewski receives no special exception—favourable or
punitive.?] [? if left_in_government = 1 and interior_minister_party !=
"Lewica": Our ministers put the written standard into coalition council and
our lawyers place monitors along the route. The serving Interior Minister must
adopt it or explain every departure; Lewica cannot command an officer through
a ministry it does not hold.?] [? if left_in_government = 0: Our lawyers
publish a shadow standard and place monitors along the route. We cannot command
an officer, but every departure by city hall or police will have a
contemporaneous public test.?]

Residents gain a procedure rather than a promise that nothing will happen.
The nationalist right loses the useful claim that only its assembly is being
governed by political discretion.

- @poland_event_queue: File the common assembly standard on the events desk

@ind24_ban
title: Press Warsaw to prohibit the nationalist march
subtitle: Ask city hall to prevent the procession and accept the legal fight that follows.
on-arrival: progressive_credibility += 3; constitutional_restraint -= 3; far_right_street_capacity += 6; braun_martyrdom += 3; konf_poll_momentum += 0.3; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support -= 3; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += 10; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_backlash += 8; news_headline = "A prohibition fight gives the march a larger national stage"

Lewica asks Warsaw to refuse the route and makes the march itself the test of
the city's anti-fascist resolve. Threatened residents hear that their fear has
not been normalised. Lawyers immediately inherit a harder question: whether
anticipated slogans and earlier incidents are enough to prohibit this year's
assembly.

Malewski moves from organiser to plaintiff and fills national broadcasts with
the litigation. Konfederacja and Braun recruit around the threatened ban; the
procession acquires more volunteers and a martyr's story before anyone steps
onto the street.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the prohibition fight on the events desk

@ko_primary_2024
# prose-audit: Grade A — Both KO contenders arrive with roles and constituencies, the incumbent counterfactual remains coherent, and each Lewica intervention retains a political relationship.
title: KO chooses its presidential candidate
subtitle: A three-way internal ballot decides who carries the democratic camp
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-trzaskowski.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 20
order: 21
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2024 and month = 11
on-arrival: {!
// An incumbent President is renominated; otherwise the ballot is genuinely
// open, and which current wins it depends on where KO's own weight now sits.
if (Q.president_name == "Rafał Trzaskowski") {
    Q.ko_primary_2024_winner = "Rafał Trzaskowski";
} else {
    const classicalWing = Number(Q.ko_classical_liberal_share) || 50;
    const socialWing = Number(Q.ko_social_liberal_share) || 50;
    const primaryWeights = {
        "Rafał Trzaskowski": 58,
        "Radosław Sikorski":
            24 + Math.max(0, classicalWing - 50) * 0.9 +
            (Q.ko_leader == "Radosław Sikorski" ? 40 : 0),
        "Barbara Nowacka":
            13 + Math.max(0, socialWing - 50) * 0.9 +
            (Q.ko_leader == "Barbara Nowacka" ? 40 : 0)
    };
    if (Q.ko_leader == "Radosław Sikorski" ||
        Q.ko_leader == "Barbara Nowacka") {
        primaryWeights["Rafał Trzaskowski"] = 22;
    }
    // 2020 still decides this ballot. A Trzaskowski who was on the ballot and
    // missed the runoff cannot be sold as the safe choice again; a
    // Trzaskowski KO refused to nominate that year is the reproach the members
    // never stopped making to themselves.
    if (Q.ko_hegemony_broken) {
        primaryWeights["Rafał Trzaskowski"] *=
            Q.pres_2020_ko_kidawa ? 1.35 : 0.45;
    }
    // Nowacka cannot contest a KO ballot from outside KO.
    if (Q.ipl_joined_left || Q.ko_2020_alliance_broken) {
        delete primaryWeights["Barbara Nowacka"];
    }
    const primaryNames = Object.keys(primaryWeights);
    const primaryTotal = primaryNames.reduce(function(sum, name) {
        return sum + primaryWeights[name];
    }, 0);
    let primaryDraw =
        (this.random.uint32() / 4294967296) * primaryTotal;
    Q.ko_primary_2024_winner = primaryNames[0];
    for (const name of primaryNames) {
        primaryDraw -= primaryWeights[name];
        if (primaryDraw <= 0) {
            Q.ko_primary_2024_winner = name;
            break;
        }
    }
}
Q.ko_primary_2024_surname =
    Q.ko_primary_2024_winner == "Radosław Sikorski" ? "Sikorski" :
    (Q.ko_primary_2024_winner == "Barbara Nowacka" ? "Nowacka" : "Trzaskowski");
Q.news_headline = Q.ko_primary_2024_winner +
    " wins KO's presidential nomination";
!}

= November 2024 — Trzaskowski, Sikorski or Nowacka

KO members choose between <span class="party-ko"><b>Rafał Trzaskowski</b></span>, [? if president_name =
"Rafał Trzaskowski": the incumbent President?][? if president_name != "Rafał
Trzaskowski": Warsaw's mayor?] and the party's 2020 presidential nominee;
<span class="party-ko"><b>Radosław Sikorski</b></span>, its foreign-policy
heavyweight and voice of a more Atlanticist, security-minded current; and
<span class="party-ko"><b>Barbara Nowacka</b></span>, the education minister
whose Inicjatywa Polska current speaks for the party's secular, social-liberal
wing. Party
leader <span class="party-ko"><b>Donald Tusk</b></span> has turned the nomination into a ballot rather than a
private designation. Lewica cannot choose KO's candidate, but it can decide
whether that candidate leaves the contest owing us anything.

[? if president_name = "Rafał Trzaskowski": In this timeline Trzaskowski
already holds the Palace. The challenge tests an incumbent shaped by five years
of cohabitation, but the decision facing us comes after the party rallies
behind the President: attach a social record to his re-election or preserve a
separate Left campaign.?]
[? if president_name != "Rafał Trzaskowski": Members give **[+
ko_primary_2024_winner +]** the nomination.?]

[? if president_name != "Rafał Trzaskowski" and ko_primary_2024_winner = "Rafał Trzaskowski": Sikorski's
substantial minority does not disappear; it becomes a network of
parliamentarians and foreign-policy figures waiting for the next KO succession
fight. We can recognise the winner, or make the ballot a public argument over
the kind of liberalism he represents.?]
[? if ko_primary_2024_winner = "Radosław Sikorski": The result puts security,
NATO and the eastern border at the centre of the democratic camp's campaign,
and puts the Left's entire social agenda a long way from it. Sikorski owes
nothing to the parties on his left and has never pretended otherwise. We can
recognise the winner, or make the ballot a public argument over the kind of
liberalism he represents.?]
[? if ko_primary_2024_winner = "Barbara Nowacka": The result is the one KO's
apparatus least wanted and our own organisers quietly hoped for: a nominee who
has spent a decade on secular schooling, reproductive rights and the parts of
the coalition programme that never reached a vote. That overlap is an
opportunity and a problem — she competes for exactly our voters. We can
recognise the winner, or make the ballot a public argument over the kind of
liberalism she represents.?]

- @ko_primary_respect
- @ko_primary_intervene
- @ko_incumbent_compact
- @ko_incumbent_distance

@ko_primary_respect
title: Respect the result and negotiate a social-policy compact
subtitle: Recognise KO's nominee in exchange for commitments on work, housing and rights.
view-if: president_name != "Rafał Trzaskowski"
on-arrival: ko_relation += 5; pres_2025_ko_candidate = ko_primary_2024_winner; pres_2025_incumbent = 0; ko_social_liberal_share += 2; ko_classical_liberal_share -= 2; news_headline = "The Left prices cooperation with KO's chosen candidate"

**[+ ko_primary_2024_surname +]** receives Lewica's congratulations together
with a written list on collective bargaining, housing and reproductive rights.
KO's social-liberal supporters use the negotiation to pull the campaign away
from a simple rerun of anti-PiS unity. The defeated currents accept the primary
result, while warning that KO has allowed a smaller party to price its
endorsement.

We have not endorsed the candidate. We have made future cooperation easier
and left a document against which both parties can be judged.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the negotiated compact on the events desk

@ko_primary_intervene
title: Publicly back the more progressive KO current
subtitle: Enter another party's contest to shift its argument, knowing its members may resent the intrusion.
view-if: president_name != "Rafał Trzaskowski"
on-arrival: pres_2025_ko_candidate = ko_primary_2024_winner; pres_2025_incumbent = 0; ko_relation -= 5; progressive_credibility += 2; ko_coalition_dissent += 4; ko_social_liberal_share += 4; ko_classical_liberal_share -= 4; news_headline = "Lewica turns KO's internal ballot into a coalition argument"

Lewica organisers publicly urge KO members to choose the current more open to
social spending and civil rights. The members vote as they were going to vote,
and **[+ ko_primary_2024_surname +]** wins anyway — but part of that mandate is
now read through our intervention. Progressives inside KO feel less isolated;
Tusk's apparatus accuses us of treating their members as an electorate we are
entitled to manage.

The nominee begins the campaign with a stronger left-facing wing and a colder
relationship with the party that helped make it visible.

- @poland_event_queue: Put KO's irritated result on the events desk

@ko_incumbent_compact
title: Back Trzaskowski's re-election for a written social and rights compact
subtitle: Share an incumbent's campaign in exchange for commitments he must defend from the Palace.
view-if: president_name = "Rafał Trzaskowski"
on-arrival: pres_2025_ko_candidate = "Rafał Trzaskowski"; pres_2025_incumbent = 1; ko_relation += 6; president_relation += 5; labor_credibility += 2; progressive_credibility += 2; trz_right_backlash += 4; pis_cohabitation_rally += 3; news_headline = "Trzaskowski seeks re-election with a negotiated social and rights compact"

The President signs a campaign compact on labour law, housing and civil
rights, and Lewica agrees to defend his re-election. Five years of vetoes,
appointments and public interventions become a shared record rather than KO's
alone. Our negotiators gain access to the Palace campaign; our own candidate
would now struggle to explain whom the Left ultimately wants to win.

PiS welcomes the clarity. It can present Trzaskowski not as a referee seeking
another term, but as the head of a democratic coalition with Lewica written
into its programme.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the presidential compact on the events desk

@ko_incumbent_distance
title: Let the incumbent run on his record and preserve a separate Left campaign
subtitle: Keep Lewica's nomination and make five years in the Palace answer for themselves.
view-if: president_name = "Rafał Trzaskowski"
on-arrival: pres_2025_ko_candidate = "Rafał Trzaskowski"; pres_2025_incumbent = 1; party_unity += 3; ko_relation -= 5; president_relation -= 2; razem_cooperation += 3; media_capacity += 1; news_headline = "The Left refuses to become the incumbent President's campaign annex"

Lewica congratulates Trzaskowski and declines the common platform. His vetoes,
appointments and compromises will be defended by his own campaign; our
nominee remains free to say where an allied President fell short. Razem and
party organisers gain a reason to work under one banner instead of becoming
canvassers for KO.

The Palace reads the distance as ingratitude after years of cohabitation. A
second-round conversation remains possible, but it will begin without the
trust a first-round compact might have bought.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the separate campaign on the events desk
